loss":"sacred duty"},{"surface":"இறுக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இறு","lemma":"இறு","gloss":"perform"},{"text":"க்கும்","lemma":"க்கும்","gloss":"habitual participle suffix"}],"gloss":"performing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முத்தீ","parts":[{"text":"முத்தீ","lemma":"முத்தீ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"விளக்கிற்","parts":[{"text":"விளக்கிற்","lemma":"விளக்கிற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"றுஞ்சும்","parts":[{"text":"றுஞ்சும்","lemma":"றுஞ்சும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பொற்கோட்டு","parts":[{"text":"பொற்கோட்டு","lemma":"பொற்கோட்டு","gloss":"golden-peaked"}],"gloss":"golden-peaked","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இமயமும்","parts":[{"text":"இமயம்","lemma":"இமயம்","gloss":"Himalayas"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the Himalayas"},{"surface":"பொதியமும்","parts":[{"text":"பொதியம்","lemma":"பொதியம்","gloss":"Podhiya hills"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the Podhiya hills"},{"surface":"போன்றே","parts":[{"text":"போன்று","lemma":"போன்று","gloss":"like"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"resembling"}]}],"literal":"Earth-packed land / and land-bearing sky / and sky-touching wind / and wind-mixed fire / and fire-opposing water, thus / like the nature of the five great elements / bearing enemies, and depth of counsel / and strength, and punishment, and grace, you possess! / Your sea-born sun again in your / white-headed wave-filled western sea sinks / in the new wealth settlements of the good country's warrior! / O Vāṉavarampaṉ, are you indeed, O great one? / With the shaking-maned horses, angry at the five / who took the land, wearing golden tumpai flowers / the hundred men having fought and perished in the battlefield, / you gave abundant food of the great feast without limit! / Even if milk sours, even if day darkens, / even if the four Vedic paths deviate, / with an unswerving retinue, shining entirely for a long time, / may you stand without trembling! On the slopes / the small-headed deer and big-eyed female deer, / at dusk, as sages perform their sacred duties, / sleep in the light of the three fires, / like the golden-peaked Himalayas and the Podhiya hills!","translation":"O king of the good country with prosperous settlements, where the sun that rises in your eastern sea sinks again in your western sea of white-crested waves! O great one, Vāṉavarampaṉ! Like the nature of the five great elements—the dense earth, the sky that rises above it, the wind that sweeps the sky, the fire mixed with the wind, and the water that opposes the fire—you possess the patience to bear enemies, the depth of counsel, strength, the power to punish, and grace. When the hundred Kauravas, wearing golden tumpai flowers, fought against the five Pandavas with shaking-maned horses for the land and perished on the battlefield, you unstintingly provided a great feast of abundant food to both sides. Even if milk sours, even if the day turns dark, and even if the four Vedas deviate from their path, may you stand unswerving with your loyal retinue, shining far and wide without trembling, like the golden-peaked Himalayas and the Podhiya hills, where on the slopes, small-headed deer and big-eyed does sleep in the light of the three fires tended by sages performing their sacred twilight duties!","modern":"மண் செறிந்த நிலமும், நிலத்தைத் தாங்கும் வானமும், வானத்தைத் தொடும் காற்றும், காற்றோடு கலந்த நெருப்பும், நெருப்பை எதிர்க்கும் நீரும் ஆகிய ஐந்து பெரும் பூதங்களின் தன்மையைப் போல, பகைவரைப் பொறுக்கும் பொறுமையும், ஆழமான ஆலோசனையும், வலிமையும், தண்டிக்கும் திறனும், அருளும் உடையவனே! உனது கிழக்குக் கடலில் தோன்றும் ஞாயிறு மீண்டும் உனது வெண்டலை அலைகளைக் கொண்ட மேற்குக்கடலில் மூழ்கும் புதிய வளங்களைக் கொண்ட நன்னாட்டின் தலைவனே! வானவரம்பனே! பெருமானே! அசையும் பிடரிமயிரைக் கொண்ட குதிரைகளையுடைய ஐவரோடு கோபித்து, நிலத்தைக் கைப்பற்ற நினைத்து, பொன்னாலான தும்பைப் பூவைச் சூடிப் போரிட்ட நூற்றுவரும் போர்க்களத்தில் மடிந்து ஒழியுமாறு, எல்லையற்ற பெருஞ்சோற்றை இருதரப்பினருக்கும் வழங்கியவனே! பால் புளித்துப் போனாலும், பகல் இருண்டு போனாலும், நான்கு வேதங்களின் நெறி மாறினாலும், நீ மட்டும் மாறாத சுற்றத்தோடு எக்காலமும் விளங்கி, நடுக்கமின்றி நிலைபெற்று வாழ்வாயாக! மலைச்சாரலில் சிறிய தலையையுடைய மான்களும் பெரிய கண்களையுடைய பெண் மான்களும், அந்திப் பொழுதில் அந்தணர்கள் தங்களது அரிய கடமைகளைச் செய்து வளர்க்கும் முத்தீயின் வெளிச்சத்தில் துயில் கொள்ளும் பொற்கோடுகளைக் கொண்ட இமயமலையும் பொதியமலையும் போல நீ நிலைத்து வாழ்வாயாக!","explanation":"The poet Murañciyūr Muṭinākarāyar addresses the Chera king Cēramāṉ Peruñcōṟṟu Utiyaṉ Cēralātaṉ in this Pāṭāṇ tiṇai poem, wishing him a long life. The poet praises the king's vast territory, stretching from the eastern sea to the western sea, and compares his virtues to the five great elements: earth (patience), sky (wisdom), wind (strength), fire (destruction), and water (grace). He also refers to the king's legendary act of feeding both the Pandavas and the Kauravas during the Mahabharata war, earning him the title 'Peruñcōṟṟu' (of the great feast). The poem concludes with a blessing for the king to stand firm and eternal like the Himalayas and the Podhiya hills, where sages perform twilight rituals and deer sleep peacefully by the sacred fires. This imagery of peaceful coexistence and cosmic order reinforces the king's role as a righteous protector.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,2.0],[2.0,2.2],[2.2,2.4],[2.4,3.8],[3.8,4.0],[4.0,4.3],[4.3,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,6.6],[6.6,6.9],[6.9,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,8.8],[8.8,9.2],[9.2,9.3],[9.3,9.7],[9.7,11.07],[11.16,11.3],[11.3,11.9],[11.9,12.3],[12.3,13.3],[13.3,13.6],[13.6,14.0],[14.0,14.3],[15.28,15.98],[15.98,16.38],[16.38,16.58],[16.58,16.78],[16.78,17.18],[17.18,18.48],[18.48,18.48],[18.48,19.08],[19.08,19.28],[19.28,20.68],[20.68,21.08],[21.08,21.18],[21.18,21.88],[21.88,22.06],[22.06,22.42],[22.48,23.08],[23.08,23.28],[23.28,24.48],[24.48,